# Differential cases (ADR-0020) of #82 and #85: objects with and without a repeated key, iterated, printed and indexed,
# around the key proof a read object's walk begins with (ADR-0044: up to 8 keys compared pairwise, more hashed, keys of
# one hash sorted; first place and last value, ADR-0002); format:
# oracle/src/main/java/io/github/subapavel/jqj/oracle/diff/DiffCase.java. Expected outputs live in distinct.rec, written
# by scripts/oracle-record.sh only. Ids are immutable. Each object of #82 runs .[] . .k0 .k8 .zz with -c.

# The 8-key boundary: 8 keys are compared pairwise, 9 are hashed (ADR-0044).

case distinct/eight-iterate
arg -c
filter .[]
stdin {"k0":0,"k1":1,"k2":2,"k3":3,"k4":4,"k5":5,"k6":6,"k7":7}\n
end

case distinct/eight-dot
arg -c
filter .
stdin {"k0":0,"k1":1,"k2":2,"k3":3,"k4":4,"k5":5,"k6":6,"k7":7}\n
end

